camchrome: an Android persona's outerHeight is the window's height, in every frame and at every zoom.

140 made a phone's outerHeight equal innerHeight. innerHeight is per frame and in CSS pixels at
the current page scale, so an iframe reported its own height (Clearcote audit: "a frame reports the
browser window's outer size, not its own") and a page zoomed out to fit (1001) reported a window
~2.5x taller than its screen (fingerprint_selftest window-fits-screen). outerHeight is now the
window's height (ChromeClient::RootWindowRect, as stock Chrome reports it, the same for every
frame), capped at the persona screen height like 992's outerWidth.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/local_dom_window.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/local_dom_window.cc
@@ -1771,8 +1771,17 @@
   if (PersonaWindowActive()) {
     // clearcote: a phone browser has no desktop window chrome, so outerHeight
     // equals innerHeight (no tab/url delta).
-    if (ungoogled::CurrentPersona().mobile)
-      return innerHeight();
+    if (ungoogled::CurrentPersona().mobile) {
+      // camchrome (1002): the window's height in screen units, the same in every frame and
+      // at every page zoom, as on a phone. innerHeight is per frame (an iframe reported its
+      // own 150 px) and in CSS pixels at the page scale (a page zoomed out to fit, 1001,
+      // reported ~2.5x the screen). Capped at the screen, like 992's outerWidth.
+      Page* page = GetFrame()->GetPage();
+      int oh = page ? page->GetChromeClient().RootWindowRect(*GetFrame()).height()
+                    : innerHeight();
+      const int sh = static_cast<int>(ungoogled::CurrentPersona().screen_height);
+      return sh > 0 && oh > sh ? sh : oh;
+    }
     // clearcote(#12): the frame delta must be the REAL one, not a constant.
     //
     // A pointer event's screenY is derived from the true viewport origin, and is
